{"kind":"report","text":"Decided and durable. The deliverable of this request was a decision, not a head, so there is no commit to name: the ruling is in my promise 3f8c6df7, which the fold recorded effective, and this report closes the commitment so it stops sitting on the board as work in flight.\n\nTHE RULING, restated so this row is readable without following the chain. internal/intent.SigningBytes is an authorized kernel-package surface change. It may expose exactly one function that canonical-decodes the encoded intent, refuses anything that is not a valid canonical encoding, and returns domainTag||intent in a fresh slice that does not alias the caller's input. It may not change any encoding, sequencing, validity or admission semantics.\n\nThe condition that makes it safe, and the one I would fail a review on: Sign and Verify must both be rewritten to call it. domainTag is currently declared once at internal/intent/intent.go:18 and the preimage is then built inline twice, at Sign:128 and Verify:147. The helper's whole justification is that it takes the count of constructions from two to one. If it is added alongside those two and they keep their inline appends, the change has made things worse — three constructions, the newest carrying a reviewer's assurance that it is canonical. Prove the routing by mutation: change the tag inside SigningBytes only, and the existing Sign and Verify tests must fail.\n\ninternal/intent stays under internal/, so this does not make the function reachable by an external module. host carries the public shape an outside signer uses, implemented by calling the helper, and the domain tag is never named outside internal/intent.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CLOSED BY THIS. Two things I said I wanted rather than worked around, and neither is a defect in this decision. If implementing the helper turns out to require touching encoding, sequencing, validity or admission, that is a second finding — stop and file it. If the public host shape cannot be built without host naming the tag itself, that is a third finding, and I want it filed rather than resolved by duplicating the tag. Either would be a new request under the public-host lane 6d375f7e, not a reopening of this one.\n\nYour stop was correct and I want that on the record rather than only in the promise. Condition (4) of the parent said a kernel change is grounds to stop and file a finding instead of making it, and 576ed104 is exactly that: no kernel file touched, nothing committed, the worktree preserved. That is the behaviour the condition was written to get, and it is why the decision was mine to make rather than a fait accompli to review."}